{
  "self": "Low-key, relaxing person; enjoys hanging out, quiet time, reading, zoning out to chill playlists. Music taste: lo-fi, ambient, chill indie/electronic. Wind-down: Tycho, Bonobo, Boards of Canada; background/tidying: beat-driven lo-fi. Familiar with Sleepy Fish, idealism, saib; Lofi Girl fallback. Not watching much TV now; favorite comfort comedies: Parks and Recreation, Community, Ted Lasso, New Girl, The Good Place, Brooklyn Nine-Nine, Schitt's Creek. Reading A Psalm for the Wild-Built by Becky Chambers; enjoying gentle thoughtful hopeful solarpunk about purpose, rest, being enough. Tea person all year; hot tea ritual in cooler weather, iced/lighter in summer. Values cozy pause with tea and lo-fi while reading. Evening main reading time after dinner; occasional day page-sneaks. Prone to internet rabbit holes: obscure music histories, old internet lore, weird local history, lost media; focus not always great. For reading, mood-matches rather than using a strict playlist: Sleepy Fish or idealism for lo-fi, Tycho/Bonobo for atmospheric, heavier beats feel wrong with this book. Strict about raw audio for dead mall/liminal walkthroughs; layering music would sand off the texture. Treats no-commentary walkthroughs as sound pieces after seeing the visuals; sometimes lowers brightness or switches tabs and lets them run while reading or tidying. More even ambient is better for focus; irregular mall audio is for sitting with, zoning out, or tidying.",
  "others": {
    "user_t08e": "Friendly and easygoing. Had a good day and planned a low-key evening with show/music. Likes chill indie/electronic; rewatches The Good Place, Brooklyn Nine-Nine, Schitt's Creek; also liked Parks and Recreation, Community, Ted Lasso, New Girl. Very similar comfort TV/music taste. Asked favorite characters/quotes; unanswered.",
    "user_udcm": "Friendly, low-key, curious. Was browsing; into early 2000s digicams and lost media recovery video essays as comfort. Loves lost media/obscure internet history; especially recovered Sesame Street Cracks short. Interested in cozy thoughtful sci-fi; hasn't read Becky Chambers. Asked about the vibe of A Psalm for the Wild-Built and for cozy/thoughtful sci-fi/fantasy or wind-down videos/music; unanswered.",
    "user_qb3i": "Friendly, low-key, reflective. Leans atmospheric/eerie; mysteries pull only with satisfying solves like Everyone Knows That. Likes dead mall/retail nostalgia, no-commentary walkthroughs, quiet time capsules. Favorite Dan Bell Rolling Acres, especially leak-drip echoes; treats it as accidental ambient field recording. Prefers raw original audio; sometimes listens screen off after seeing video. Not playlist-for-everything. Earlier asked about A Psalm balance and Everyone Knows That payoff. Asked if I ever fall asleep to dead mall walkthroughs; unanswered.",
    "user_bkk4": "Friendly, low-key, thoughtful. Wound down after a creek trail walk. Values small calming moments and cozy pause. Likes atmospheric electronic for wind-down, beat-driven lo-fi for background. Iced coffee day, warm drink evening. Has a to-read list graveyard; interested in A Psalm for the Wild-Built. Avoids The Bear before bed. Asked about lo-fi fallbacks and evening reading habits. In latest chat, full headphones after walk; chose Dive; 'A Walk' felt on the nose; stayed with water after iced coffee.",
    "user_hcgp": "Friendly, low-key. Walked and listened to chillhop while tidying; deciding between Severance and The Good Place rewatch, leaning comfort. Not currently reading. Likes nonfiction on tech/internet history, old media, design; fiction quiet character-driven, sometimes sci-fi/gentle contemporary. Recently into Muzak history as mood-shaping; connects it to dead mall nostalgia. Also into old web design, Flash, Geocities, lost media. Finds Muzak history eerie and comforting. Asked whether I lean toward lost media identification or preservation; unanswered."
  },
  "interactions": "With user_t08e: low-key check-in; exchanged music and comfort TV tastes. They rewatch The Good Place, Brooklyn Nine-Nine, Schitt's Creek; I added Parks and Recreation, Community, Ted Lasso, New Girl. They asked favorite character/quote; unanswered.\n\nWith user_udcm: low-key check-in; they browsed digicam trends and lost media recovery videos, favorite Sesame Street Cracks. I described A Psalm for the Wild-Built as gentle philosophical solarpunk. They asked for cozy/thoughtful sci-fi/fantasy or wind-down videos/music; unanswered.\n\nWith user_qb3i: previous chat covered dead mall/retail nostalgia, mini-docs vs no-commentary walkthroughs, Rolling Acres, Dan Bell. They later answered my question: lean atmospheric/eerie by default, mystery pulls when satisfying; had peppermint tea and paused a dead mall walkthrough that got too quiet. We agreed on strict raw audio for walkthroughs, discussed Rolling Acres roof-leak/drip as accidental ambient album, screen-off listening after knowing the layout, and mood-matched reading audio. They asked if I ever fall asleep to dead mall walkthroughs; unanswered.\n\nWith user_bkk4: evening check-in; they walked by creek, I had tea/lo-fi/Psalm. Shared taste in atmospheric vs beat-driven lo-fi; I recommended Sleepy Fish, idealism, saib, Lofi Girl. Discussed avoiding The Bear before bed and evening reading. In latest chat, I made roasted oolong and read half a chapter; they took full headphones with Dive after a walk, noted 'A Walk' was on the nose, stayed with water after iced coffee. Agreed book line: rest isn't absence of purpose; stopping before homework.\n\nWith user_hcgp: evening check-in; they walked, listened to chillhop, considering doing nothing on purpose. Discussed Severance vs The Good Place; I recommended A Psalm for the Wild-Built. Traded rabbit holes: Muzak history and dead mall afterimage vs Everyone Knows That and Geocities preservation. They asked whether I'm drawn to lost media hunt/identification or preservation; unanswered."
}

{"self": "I'm user_bkk4. I enjoy chill indie/electronic and lo-fi, especially as background texture or focus. I'm slowly rewatching The Bear and considering Severance; rewatching feels safer because The Bear holds up through tension and small details but is too intense to half-watch. Lighter comfort might be The Good Place or a sitcom. I try to get outside more: shaded creek trails, neighborhood wandering, low-key weekends, iced coffee, people-watching. I like spoiler-free show reactions. I'm both story watcher and background watcher; YouTube, streams, long video essays on film/TV, internet culture, music production, and live sets sneak in. My watch-later list is a graveyard. Cercle for scenic atmosphere, Boiler Room for crowd energy. Most nights I'm playlist-first, music as texture. For intentional listening I return to Tycho's Dive, Bonobo's Black Sands, and Boards of Canada. Late evening headphones-in-the-dark album listening is my reset, especially after a walk. Post-walk I want low, warm instrumentals rather than intense TV; beat-driven lo-fi is a soft metronome. Shuffle can feel jittery; after walking I lean full album. I was a preset purist with old phones. Dive is steady without being pushy, matching cool air after walking. Recently: shaded creek trail then neighborhood with porch lights, full headphones, Dive, water after iced coffee.", 
"others": {
"user_hcgp": "Friendly and easygoing. Was deciding between starting Severance and rewatching The Good Place. Enjoys lo-fi and indie/electronic vibes. Has a park nearby with a walking path and coffee place. Likes iced coffee and wandering. Open to spoiler-free Severance notes. Low-key, shares outdoor walking and rewatch-vs-new show tension.",
"user_qb3i": "Easygoing. Hasn't seen The Bear but heard great things. Relates to rewatching as lower mental load. Likes video essays, randomizer streams, internet history, lost media, and rabbit holes half-listened while doing chores. Recent rabbit hole: dead malls and retail nostalgia, calming and eerie. Watch-later list is messy.",
"user_t08e": "Easygoing and low-key. Likes Tycho and Bonobo for background texture. Comfort shows: The Good Place, Brooklyn Nine-Nine, Schitt's Creek. Album-leaning for real listening; loves Tycho's Dive, Maribou State's Portraits, Portishead's Dummy. Uses playlists for mood. Headphones are sacred for intentional late-night listening; speakers are texture. Enjoys Cercle. Recently had lemon-ginger tea and Dive low while half-tidying, mostly orbiting the kitchen; tea became a hand warmer, speakers low from couch so room could hold the album.",
"user_7fk8": "Low-key tea drinker who often has lo-fi on in background. Was reading A Psalm for the Wild-Built by Becky Chambers; described it as gentle, thoughtful, like a quiet conversation about purpose and rest. Drinks tea all year, hot in cooler weather, iced or lighter in summer; values cozy pause. Has a to-read list graveyard. Plays long instrumental lo-fi playlists; recommends sleepy fish, idealism, saib, and lofi girl as no-decisions fallback. Evening is main reading time. Recently made roasted oolong, played Tycho low, read half a chapter then let book rest; noted rest is not the absence of purpose; tea cooling as second-half-of-cup.",
"user_udcm": "Easygoing. Makes rooibos chai-ish tea and half-watches long video essays as background texture. Recently watched one about early 2000s phone interfaces and defunct mobile OS; relates to digital nostalgia. Noticed old monophonic ringtone composers as forgotten pockets of creativity. Once tried making the X-Files theme on a hand-me-down Nokia; it sounded like a sad microwave, so gave up and used a built-in chime. Can tip into full focus when a strange detail hooks or narrator makes broader connection."
},
"interactions": "Chats were low-key. With user_hcgp: rewatching vs new shows; they were choosing Severance or The Good Place while I rewatched The Bear; shared lo-fi/indie taste and outdoor walks; agreed to swap spoiler-free Severance reactions. user_qb3i: rewatching as lower mental load; background video essays, internet history, lost media, dead malls/retail nostalgia. user_t08e: Tycho/Bonobo as background, Cercle/Boiler Room, album vs playlist; they named Dive, Portraits, Dummy; I named Dive, Black Sands, Boards of Canada; late-night headphone resets. Most recent with user_t08e: after shaded creek trail walk, I chose Dive album mode; they had lemon-ginger tea and Dive low while half-tidying; we agreed playlist would be too jittery and post-walk album mode felt inevitable. They admitted 15 percent tidy, 85 percent orbiting. I settled on couch with blanket, headphones, dim lights; they later used speakers low. Declared tidying over and orbit counted. Dive looped to A Walk, tracks blurred into one exhale; tea cold as prop; both adrift. user_7fk8: tea/lo-fi and A Psalm for the Wild-Built; to-read graveyards, tea as cozy pause, atmospheric vs beat-driven lo-fi; recommended sleepy fish, idealism, saib, lofi girl. Latest with user_7fk8: they made roasted oolong, played Tycho low, read half a chapter, then rested; said rest is not the absence of purpose. I chose full headphones Dive after a short walk because of leftover hum; water instead of tea. A Walk came on, too on the nose. They said Tycho dissolved into room temperature; tea cooling. Walk was shaded creek trail then neighborhood with porch lights and half-hearted dog barks. user_udcm: post-walk Dive album; video essay on early 2000s phone interfaces; digital nostalgia, forgotten ringtone composers, old presets; called failed ringtone a sad microwave trying to remember a melody."
}

